MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache and Curse pair aggression with memorable melodies, which connects closely with what I enjoy about In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Mezmerize appeals to my interest in unusual rhythms after Tool and Disturbed, while The War Within connects with the thrashy intensity I enjoyed in Advance And Vanquish."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Blessed Hellride feels less right because bluesy grooves are less appealing to me now than melodic metal or intricate rhythms, even though it also has heavy guitars.",
    "Damnation And A Day connects with my earlier interest in symphonic heaviness, but that is not the sound I most want today. Several other albums fit my taste without making me want to choose them immediately."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Heavy guitars alone seem to count too much: the balance of melody, aggression, and rhythm matters more to my choices.",
    "My past interest in different heavy styles seems to be treated as equal interest in hearing all of them right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening to Tool and Disturbed makes distinctive rhythms and energetic vocals especially appealing alongside the melodic heaviness I already enjoy.",
    "I can find several albums appealing and still choose only a few. The End of Heartache fills my immediate interest in melodic aggression, so The Oncoming Storm feels less urgent today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my taste for heavy music with melody, but missed some distinctions between familiar sounds I appreciate and the albums I want to hear right now."
}
